  [1mClassification: architectural, not bounded.[0m I want to flag why, since the edit looks small. "Reusable across multiple
  forms" names structure this repo doesn't have — a shared validation module, a rule/schema format, and consumers (the
  other forms) that don't exist yet. Bounded means the flow I'd change is already here to read; here there's exactly one
  form and no shared layer. There's also a real seam to resolve: [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is a plain [38;5;153m<script>[39m with no module system while
  [38;5;153msrc/[39m is CommonJS, so "put validation in a shared module" has to answer how the browser loads it. So I'll run the full
  process — questions, approaches, a sectioned design, then a written spec — rather than presenting a two-sentence
  design.

